## From Text to Tokens

```
Source: fn main() -> Int { return 42; }

Tokens:
  FN          (keyword 'fn')
  IDENT(main) (identifier)
  LPAREN      (
  RPAREN      )
  ARROW       (->)
  IDENT(Int)  (type name)
  LBRACE      (
  RETURN      (keyword 'return')
  INT(42)     (integer literal)
  SEMICOLON   (;
  RBRACE      (})
```

### Lexer Architecture

```xiom
pub type Lexer = {
  source: Str;
  pos: Int;      // Current position
  line: Int;     // Current line
  col: Int;      // Current column
}

impl Lexer {
  fn next_token(self: &mut Lexer) -> Token {
    self.skip_whitespace();
    if self.is_eof() { return Token::EOF; }

    let c = self.current_char();
    return match c {
      '(' => { self.advance(); Token::LParen },
      ')' => { self.advance(); Token::RParen },
      '-' => {
        self.advance();
        if self.current_char() == '>' {
          self.advance();
          Token::Arrow
        } else { Token::Minus }
      },
      'a'..='z' | 'A'..='Z' | '_' => self.lex_identifier(),
      '0'..='9' => self.lex_number(),
      '"' => self.lex_string(),
      _ => {
        let ch = self.current_char();
        self.advance();
        Token::Error("Unexpected character: " + ch.to_str())
      },
    };
  }
}
```

### Token Types

```xiom
pub enum Token {
  // Keywords
  Fn, Let, Return, If, Else, While, For, Match, Pub,
  // Literals
  IntLiteral(value: Int),
  FloatLiteral(value: Float64),
  StrLiteral(value: Str),
  CharLiteral(value: Char),
  BoolLiteral(value: Bool),
  // Identifiers
  Identifier(name: Str),
  // Operators
  Plus, Minus, Star, Slash, Percent,
  // Delimiters
  LParen, RParen, LBrace, RBrace, LBracket, RBracket, Semicolon, Comma, Colon,
  Arrow, FatArrow,
  // Special
  EOF,
  Error(message: Str),
}
```

### Performance

The lexer is the FASTEST compiler phase — designed to process megabytes per second. It uses a deterministic finite automaton (DFA) internally for O(n) performance.

